# Review: NavTreePlugin

The plugin implements almost everything the spec describes. Tab switching, selection, drag-and-drop and
expansion all live in `NavTreeContainer`; per-path state is in the `State` capability; shortcuts are in the
`Keyboard` capability; `expose` is a handler for `LayoutOperation.Expose`. Tests cover the keyboard
bindings and `expose` (`plugin.browser.test.ts`), drop-kind resolution and rearrange indices
(`util.test.ts`), open-state persistence (`nav-tree-view-state.test.ts`) and focus/selection via the
`NavTree` stories. Tab switching, the option/active-item selection branches, the drop callbacks and current
tracking have no test.

Divergences: persistence goes through the attention plugin's `ViewState` `local` backend rather than a
hand-rolled localStorage blob (same effect). Teardown unregisters only the plugin's own hotkeys, not a
`Keyboard.singleton` (F-5.4). `keyBinding` lives on action properties, not `NodeProperties`.

Of 43 items: 12 done, 20 untested, 8 partial, 1 diverged, 2 missing.

